Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='agentrecord', at=datetime(2026, 10, 24, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title="The fence has a type behind it: the agent's verbs are pure handlers over an Agent record with nothing outward", body='*The fence has a type behind it*. The verbs are `suzatary mcp` (`app/cli/src/commands/mcp.rs`): pure handlers in `suzatary_core::agent` over an `Agent` record — chain, mail corpus, mailbox, the repository\'s gates, manuals, renderer, clock, and the secretary\'s memory read-only (eight fields, the last a `secretary::recollection::Recollection`, whose stores are private and whose every method reads; 2026-10-24; a record is a list of authorities, one trait per effect, passed as a value) — and nothing outward. "No send tool" and "no confirm twin" are facts about what typechecks; the verb list is closed and snapshotted; every write\'s actor is the constant `agent::WRITES_AS` (`Writer::Triage`), which no argument reaches, so a forged trusted origin cannot be expressed. `tool-guard.sh` stays as the belt. Reads come back as curated context (`context`, `todo_show`, `list_open_todos`, and the memory\'s `recall` and `zoom`), writes as verbs (`todo_add`, `todo_update`, `record`).', rationale="The eighth field, the secretary's memory read-only, was added 2026-10-24.", supersedes=()))